{"id":"y9-2-2-loops","label":"2.2: Loops and Combined Constructs","steps":[{"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Question 1","type":"exam-do-now","questionSetKey":"y10-1-1-l3-plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A recap question from Unit 1, Number Systems: hexadecimal to denary.</p><div id=\"donow-root\"></div>"},{"id":"do-now-2","label":"Do Now: Question 2","type":"exam-do-now","questionSetKey":"y10-1-1-l2","trackingSuffix":"-2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">One more from Unit 1: denary to binary.</p><div id=\"donow-root\"></div>"},{"id":"title","label":"Loops and Combined Constructs","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithm Design and Text Programming</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Loops and Combined Constructs</h2><p>Year 9, 2.2</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Concept:</strong> The count-controlled loop: FOR ... TO ... NEXT.</li><li><strong>Activity 1:</strong> Trace a loop in a trace table and predict what it outputs.</li><li><strong>Activity 2:</strong> Write loops that are run and checked straight away.</li><li><strong>Also today:</strong> Putting decisions inside loops.</li></ul>"},{"id":"concept","label":"Count-Controlled Loops","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Count-Controlled Loops</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A count-controlled loop repeats its lines a set number of times. In Cambridge pseudocode it is written FOR ... TO ... NEXT.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 5</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Hello\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>The <strong>counter</strong> (Count) must be declared first, as an INTEGER.</li><li>Count starts at the first value (1) and goes up by 1 on each pass, up to the last value (5).</li><li>The lines between FOR and NEXT run once per pass: here, 5 times.</li><li>Number of passes = last value &minus; first value + 1.</li></ul>"},{"id":"check-loops","label":"Check: Reading a FOR Loop","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9l22-check-loops","validatorKey":"y9l22_check_loops","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Reading a FOR Loop</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Use this loop for parts (a) and (b).</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 3 TO 9</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-check-loops-a\">(a) How many times does the loop run? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-check-loops-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-loops-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Reading a FOR Loop part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-check-loops-b\">(b) What is the last value this loop outputs? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-check-loops-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-loops-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Reading a FOR Loop part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-check-loops-c\">(c) Write the FOR line for a loop where Count goes from 1 to 20. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-check-loops-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-loops-c\" aria-label=\"Check: Reading a FOR Loop part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l22-check-loops-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l22-check-loops-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"worked","label":"Worked Example: Trace a Loop","type":"embedded-app","appId":"trace-table-practice","embedContainerId":"y9l22-embed-worked","embedQuery":"view=walkthrough&lang=cambridge","embedView":"walkthrough","algorithm":{"title":"Adding in a Loop","context":"Step through the program one line at a time and watch the trace table fill in.","code":["DECLARE Total : INTEGER","DECLARE Count : INTEGER","Total = 0","for Count in range(1, 4):","    Total = Total + 5","print(Total)"],"cols":["Line","Total","Count","Output"],"answers":[{"Line":"3","Total":"0","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Total":"","Count":"1","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Total":"5","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Total":"","Count":"2","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Total":"10","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Total":"","Count":"3","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Total":"15","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"6","Total":"","Count":"","Output":"15"}]},"content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Worked Example: Trace a Loop</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Step through the loop and watch Count and Total change on every pass.</p><div id=\"y9l22-embed-worked\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-1","label":"Activity 1: Trace a Loop","type":"embedded-app","appId":"trace-table-practice","embedContainerId":"y9l22-embed-1","embedQuery":"view=practice&lang=cambridge&support=1","embedView":"practice","algorithm":{"title":"Doubling in a Loop","context":"Complete the trace table for this program.","code":["DECLARE Score : INTEGER","DECLARE Count : INTEGER","Score = 1","for Count in range(1, 5):","    Score = Score * 2","print(Score)"],"cols":["Line","Score","Count","Output"],"answers":[{"Line":"3","Score":"1","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Score":"","Count":"1","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Score":"2","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Score":"","Count":"2","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Score":"4","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Score":"","Count":"3","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Score":"8","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"4","Score":"","Count":"4","Output":""},{"Line":"5","Score":"16","Count":"","Output":""},{"Line":"6","Score":"","Count":"","Output":"16"}]},"content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 1: Trace a Loop</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Fill in a row whenever a variable changes or something is output.</p><div id=\"y9l22-embed-1\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"},{"id":"exam-errors","label":"Exam Question: Find the Errors (1 of 2)","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9l22-exam-errors","validatorKey":"y9l22_exam_errors","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Find the Errors</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This algorithm should input the 5 digits of a number, one at a time, and total each digit multiplied by its position (the first digit is in position 1). It contains two errors.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Digit : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 10</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Please enter digit \", Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Digit</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">08&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total + (Digit / Count)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">09&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">10&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"The total is \", Total</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-exam-errors-a\">(a) Give the line number of the error in the loop. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-errors-a\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-exam-errors-b\">(b) Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-errors-b\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, October/November 2025 Paper 21, Question 6(a)</p></div></div>"},{"id":"exam-errors-2","label":"Exam Question: Find the Errors (2 of 2)","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9l22-exam-errors-2","validatorKey":"y9l22_exam_errors_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Find the Errors</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This algorithm should input the 5 digits of a number, one at a time, and total each digit multiplied by its position (the first digit is in position 1). It contains two errors.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Digit : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 10</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Please enter digit \", Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Digit</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">08&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total + (Digit / Count)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">09&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">10&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"The total is \", Total</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-exam-errors-2-a\">(a) Give the line number of the other error. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-errors-2-a\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-exam-errors-2-b\">(b) Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-errors-2-b\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l22-exam-errors-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, October/November 2025 Paper 21, Question 6(a)</p></div></div>"},{"id":"concept-2","label":"Decisions Inside Loops","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Decisions Inside Loops</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Real programs combine all three constructs: sequence, selection (IF) and iteration (FOR).</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Passes : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Mark : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Passes &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 5</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Mark</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Mark &gt;= 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Passes &larr; Passes + 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Passes</div></div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Before the loop:</strong> set the starting value once (Passes &larr; 0).</li><li><strong>Inside the loop:</strong> the IF is checked on every pass, but Passes only goes up when it is TRUE.</li><li><strong>After the loop:</strong> output the result once, when the loop has finished.</li></ul></div>"},{"id":"check-combine","label":"Check: Decisions Inside Loops","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9l22-check-combine","validatorKey":"y9l22_check_combine","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Decisions Inside Loops</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This program runs, and the user types 45, 60, 50, 38, 72.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Passes : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Mark : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Passes &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 5</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Mark</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Mark &gt;= 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Passes &larr; Passes + 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Passes</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-check-combine-a\">(a) What does the program output? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-check-combine-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-combine-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Decisions Inside Loops part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-check-combine-b\">(b) How many times is the IF condition checked? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-check-combine-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-combine-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Decisions Inside Loops part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-check-combine-c\">(c) Should Passes <- 0 go before, inside or after the loop? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-check-combine-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"check-combine-c\" aria-label=\"Check: Decisions Inside Loops part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l22-check-combine-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l22-check-combine-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"activity-2","label":"Activity 2: Write the Loop","type":"embedded-app","appId":"drill-y9-2-2-code","embedContainerId":"y9l22-embed-2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 2: Write the Loop</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write each program in Cambridge pseudocode. It is run with test values and checked straight away.</p><div id=\"y9l22-embed-2\"></div>"},{"id":"practice","label":"Checked Practice","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9l22-practice","validatorKey":"y9l22_practice","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Checked Practice</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Score : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Score &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Count &lt;= 2 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Score &larr; Score + 3</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Score &larr; Score + 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Score</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-practice-a\">(a) Predict what this program outputs. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-practice-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"practice-a\" aria-label=\"Checked Practice part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l22-practice-b\">(b) A loop must run exactly 6 times, starting at 4. What number goes after TO? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l22-practice-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"practice-b\" aria-label=\"Checked Practice part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l22-practice-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l22-practice-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Loops and Combined Constructs","type":"embedded-app","appId":"drill-y9-2-2-loops","embedContainerId":"y9l22-plenary-drill","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Loops and Combined Constructs</h2><div id=\"y9l22-plenary-drill\"></div>"}],"validators":{"y9l22_check_loops":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*7(\\s*times?)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Count takes 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 9: that is 9 - 3 + 1 = 7 passes."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*9\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The last pass is when Count equals the TO value, 9."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*for\\s+count\\s*(<-|←)\\s*1\\s+to\\s+20\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"FOR, the counter, the arrow and the first value, then TO and the last value: FOR Count <- 1 TO 20."}],"y9l22_exam_errors":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(line\\s*)?0?5\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Line 05: a 5-digit number needs 5 passes, but the loop runs 10 times."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*for\\s+count\\s*(<-|←)\\s*1\\s+to\\s+5\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"FOR Count <- 1 TO 5 runs once for each of the 5 digits."}],"y9l22_exam_errors_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(line\\s*)?0?8\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Line 08: each digit should be MULTIPLIED by its position, not divided."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*total\\s*(<-|←)\\s*total\\s*\\+\\s*(\\(\\s*digit\\s*\\*\\s*count\\s*\\)|digit\\s*\\*\\s*count|\\(\\s*count\\s*\\*\\s*digit\\s*\\)|count\\s*\\*\\s*digit)\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Total <- Total + (Digit * Count): * multiplies, / divides."}],"y9l22_check_combine":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*3\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"60, 50 and 72 are 50 or more (50 counts, because >= includes it): 3 passes."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*5(\\s*times?)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The IF is inside the loop, so it is checked on all 5 passes."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(it\\s+(goes|should\\s+go)\\s+)?before(\\s+the\\s+loop)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Before the loop: inside it, Passes would be reset to 0 on every pass."}],"y9l22_practice":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*10\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Count 1 and 2 take the THEN branch (+3 each), Count 3 and 4 take ELSE (+2 each): 3 + 3 + 2 + 2 = 10."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*9\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Pass 1 is 4, so pass 6 is 9: FOR Count <- 4 TO 9."}]},"pseudocodeValidators":{}}